        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"PWM\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"6\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"6\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"SDA\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"5\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"5\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"RST\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"1\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "an ATtiny-driven fan controller"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If both MCUs are populated, their GPIO outputs can contend on shared lines such as PWM, potentially causing incorrect fan control or electrical stress. The files show no circuitry to select or isolate one MCU.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist connects two separately footprinted ATtiny MCUs directly in parallel across the fan-control signals, with no shown selection or isolation. If both are populated, their GPIOs can conflict."
}

